  "Id": 1114,
  "Title": "\u200bWorkshop upgrades teachers' skills in maths",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "\u200bThe Mathematics Association of Pakistan (MAP) recently held its first workshop for teachers covering the O'Level Mathematics syllabus at The Aga Khan University Institute for Educational Development. ",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<div class=\"ExternalClassA310B95ABF2544508316DEA8FF39DBA6\"><div>\u200bThe Mathematics Association of Pakistan (MAP) recently held its first workshop for teachers covering the O'Level Mathematics syllabus at The Aga Khan University Institute for Educational Development. Held at the request of educators, thirty-two teachers from government and private schools in Karachi attended the four-day workshop.</div><div><br></div><div>It provided an opportunity for teachers to upgrade their skills in teaching the Mathematics O'Level syllabus. Participating teachers learnt about each other's work and school environments. Experienced O'Level teachers led the workshop.</div><div><br></div><div>The workshop was part of MAP's efforts to create a supportive environment for the professional development of mathematics teachers in Pakistan. MAP holds regular workshops for teachers with the overall aim of improving the quality of education in Pakistan.</div></div>",
